--
N5008 [temp.variadic]/5,7: a class template's member operator()(A... args)
whose body expands the class pack (forward<A>(args)...) for an EMPTY pack
-- the parameter disappears, and the body's expansion must be recorded as
zero elements (it was not recorded when the class pack expansion happened
at substitution time, so 'args' stayed in the body: every
std::function<R()> call operator was bodiless).  Also a member typedef of a
function-pointer type whose pointee expands the class pack
(`typedef R (*invoker_t)(const any_data &, A &&...)`, libstdc++'s
_Invoker_type spelled with typedef) must expand it like a data member.
